B.bvX=new A.k("In Flutter Material-2 the default dialog background color is surface for all Dialogs. In Material-3 mode they default to surfaceContainerHigh. FCS 8.0 and later uses surfaceContainerHigh in both modes.\nYou can theme dialogs to a different color scheme color. It is recommended to stick to one of the surface colors.\n\nThe AlertDialog uses the general DialogTheme for theming values. TimePicker and DatePicker have their own themes. In the Themes Playground they share the same setting for the background color, but you can change them individually in the produced code.\n",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
