B.bua=new A.k('Use tone 30 instead of 10 for onColors on containers in LIGHT mode. This is the Material-3 spec standard used by Flutter 3.47+ ColorScheme.fromSeed. It is more color expressive, but reduces contrast.\n\nFlexColorScheme 9.0 defaults this ON so seeded light themes match ColorScheme.fromSeed. Turn it OFF to keep the older higher-contrast tone 10 on-container colors. Flutter ColorScheme.fromSeed has no such opt-out.\n\nThis modifier ONLY impacts LIGHT scheme variants where the container on colors use tone 10. Dark mode already uses expressive on-container tones (tone 90). For scheme variants with an intentionally custom tone for onColors on containers, this setting has no impact. Such variants are:\n - Fidelity\n - Monochrome\n - Content\n - Ultra Contrast\n - Candy pop\n - Chroma\n\nFor MCU seed generated schemes, this only has any impact when contrast level is at the default value (0), normal contrast.\n\nWhen using FSS seed generated schemes, the tones modifier "B&W main onColors" will override this setting.\n',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
